# Keep it fast

Whenever you add or change features in this project, treat frame rate as a first-class requirement (especially on Windows).

## Do

- Prefer `MeshLambertMaterial` / `MeshBasicMaterial` over `MeshStandardMaterial` unless a single hero mesh truly needs it
- Reuse materials and geometries; avoid allocating new mats/geos per frame
- Cap decorative extras (escorts, particles, lights, window meshes) — fewer, cheaper instances
- Use simpler LOD / low-poly for background or escort vehicles; detail only on the player vehicle
- Avoid per-frame `traverse`, material dispose thrash, and unnecessary lights (PointLights are expensive)
- After visual upgrades, immediately trim cost (counts, segments, transparency, shadows)

## Don't

- Don't add dozens of transparent Standard-material panes "for realism" without a cheap path
- Don't spawn heavy full-detail meshes for AI/escort traffic
- Don't leave performance for a follow-up — optimize in the same change
